{
  "name": "anaconda",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/herps/snakes.py): the GREEN ANACONDA, Eunectes murinus, 5 m and 24 cm thick -- the heaviest snake, its weight resting on the ground, the tail an eighth of it; a narrow head barely wider than the neck, the EYES AND NOSTRILS HIGH ON THE CROWN (it lies awash), vertical pupils; olive green with PAIRED BLACK OVAL BLOTCHES down the back, black rings with yellow middles in a row along each flank, an orange stripe from the eye back to the jaw between two black ones, a yellowish belly spotted black. Coats: green, yellow anaconda (E. notaeus, .7), dark. A slow heavy crawl.",
